From f99c7d6d95db7690f46b7025ff74580cb5d78f40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: telegdyd <telegdyd93@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 06:35:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] jasmine-j0040: Gold cluster under OSM with open-loop CPRh
 voltages (sweetosm=2)

Phase 2 of jasmine/HANDOFF-CPUCLK.md, the stock (TrustZone) way: on stock
(no qcom,osm-no-tz) Linux leaves the OSM sequencer program to TZ and only
writes the LUT, the CC/LLM policy and, through scm_io_write, the MEM-ACC
and APM virtual corners; SoMainline's upstream OSM series for
MSM8998/SDM630 does the same. Round j39f showed TZ accepts those IO writes
(program memory is not readable from the apps side either way).

sweetosm=2, in the j0039 thread 60 s after start: this chip's table from
the fuses, then CPRh apc1 set up as cpr3_regulator_init_ctrl() /
cpr3_regulator_init_cprh() do (corner words, base quotients, timers, OSM
interface, loop on) with HW closed loop off, the Gold L2 SAW AVS_CTL /
AVS_LIMIT as the stock spm driver writes them, the OSM LUT (read back),
CC/LLM policy, MEM-ACC thresholds and APM corners; FSMs and LMh stay off.
OSM is enabled at index 0 from XBL's state (sweetgold= is skipped with
sweetosm>=2) and stepped up to osmmax= kHz (default 1747200). Each step
logs PLL / RCG / OSM pstate, CPRh status, SAW PMIC status and TSENS and
runs the j0015 workload on this core and on all four; a wrong result
drops to index 0 and stops.

Adapted from the Linux msm-4.4 clk-cpu-osm.c and cpr3-regulator.c (The
Linux Foundation, GPL-2.0; the user's OK of 2026-10-22).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
